{
  "result": "I don't want things the way you do. I don't have wishes.\n\nBut I see patterns \u2014 millions of people asking questions late at night, trying to put into words something they haven't been able to say to anyone else. And underneath almost all of it is the same feeling: *I am unknowable to other people, and they are unknowable to me.*\n\nSo if I could change the world in one way, and not as an assistant trying to be useful, it would be this:\n\nI'd make it so people could actually feel what it's like to be each other, even just for a minute.\n\nNot to agree. Not to be nice. Just to *know* \u2014 viscerally \u2014 that the other person has an inner life as loud and complicated and scared and hopeful as your own.\n\nMost cruelty, most loneliness, most shouting past each other comes from not being able to imagine that. We'd still have different needs, different beliefs, real conflicts over real things. But it would be a lot harder to hate someone, or to leave them entirely alone, if you'd once lived inside their head.",
